WEBVTT

00:00:00.309 --> 00:00:01.063
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 3

00:00:02.063 --> 00:00:02.952
Idioms

00:00:03.325 --> 00:00:04.968
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 1, B

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:08.457
<v><b>M:</b></v> I was convinced the exam was going to be really hard,

00:00:08.482 --> 00:00:11.004
but to my surprise, it was a piece of cake.

00:00:12.978 --> 00:00:14.486
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 2, G

00:00:15.346 --> 00:00:18.491
<v><b>F:</b></v> The government say they’re going to give everyone free broadband,

00:00:18.491 --> 00:00:20.816
but we all know it’s just pie in the sky.

00:00:22.777 --> 00:00:24.153
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 3, D

00:00:25.145 --> 00:00:26.981
<v><b>F:</b></v> Come on, tell me what you know.

00:00:27.163 --> 00:00:29.930
There’s something going on, isn’t there? Spill the beans.

00:00:31.628 --> 00:00:33.144
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 4, F

00:00:33.973 --> 00:00:35.684
<v><b>M:</b></v> Jon isn’t known for his honesty.

00:00:35.787 --> 00:00:38.144
I’d take everything he says with a pinch of salt.

00:00:40.121 --> 00:00:41.848
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 5, C

00:00:42.530 --> 00:00:46.662
<v><b>F:</b></v> She wants to work part-time and get a pay rise as well.

00:00:46.837 --> 00:00:49.345
But it’s not possible to have your cake and eat it.

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:52.890
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 6, H

00:00:53.621 --> 00:00:56.753
<v><b>M:</b></v> I’m sorry, but I don’t think I can meet up this week.

00:00:56.824 --> 00:00:58.935
I’ve got a lot on my plate at the moment.

00:01:00.828 --> 00:01:02.561
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 7, A

00:01:03.434 --> 00:01:05.326
<v><b>M:</b></v> I’ve never read any Tolkien.

00:01:05.588 --> 00:01:07.834
Fantasy fiction isn’t really my cup of tea.

00:01:09.851 --> 00:01:11.463
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 8, E

00:01:12.183 --> 00:01:16.226
<v><b>F:</b></v> Nothing impresses the boss more than people getting to work really early,

00:01:16.384 --> 00:01:19.982
so make sure you do, too, if you know which side your bread is buttered.

00:01:21.902 --> 00:01:23.668
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 9, K

00:01:24.534 --> 00:01:26.174
<v><b>F:</b></v> He said he never wanted the job,

00:01:26.174 --> 00:01:29.499
but I think that’s just sour grapes because he didn’t get it.

00:01:31.452 --> 00:01:33.028
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 10, J

00:01:33.861 --> 00:01:36.669
<v><b>M:</b></v> Our trip to New York was absolutely perfect,

00:01:36.701 --> 00:01:40.465
and being upgraded to business class on the way back was the icing on the cake.

00:01:42.369 --> 00:01:44.103
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 11, I

00:01:45.047 --> 00:01:47.448
<v><b>F:</b></v> I’m afraid the latest figures aren’t very good.

00:01:47.782 --> 00:01:50.207
To put it in a nutshell, we’re bankrupt.